INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES
('wolverine-people', 'Wolverine People', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any; most are Scrupulous (50%), Unprincipled (20%), Principled (10%) or Anarchist (10%).', '{"IQ":"1D6+10","ME":"2D6+3","MA":"2D6+10","PS":"2D6+22","PP":"2D6+10","PE":"2D6+11","PB":"2D6+5","Spd":"3D6+3"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx10+1D6+10', '4D6', 'MEx3+1D6', 'A Mega-Damage creature; the row rolls a male. Male M.D.C. is P.E. x10 plus 1D6+10 per level of experience; female M.D.C. is P.E. x9 plus 9 per level. P.P.E. 4D6 for males, 5D6 for females. I.S.P. is M.E. x3 plus 1D6 per level. Female attributes: I.Q. 1D6+11, M.E. 2D6+4, M.A. 2D6+12, P.S. 2D6+17 (Robotic), P.P. 3D6+10, P.E. 2D6+9, P.B. 3D6+8, Spd 3D6+9. P.S. is Robotic for both. Natural A.R. 15 applies only in S.D.C. settings.', 15, 12, '{"perception":1,"strike":1,"parry":1,"dodge":1,"roll":2}', 'Attacks per melee come from the Hand to Hand skill (Basic unless a military package upgrades it), +1 at level 5 for males and +1 at levels 2, 8 and 16 for females. Racial bonuses: +1 Perception, +1 strike, parry and dodge, +2 roll with impact; females add +1 initiative and +1 more Perception. Horror Factor saves: -2 against the supernatural (-4 if wild-born), +1 against every other threat. Facing demons, Entities, ghosts, spirits or gods: -1 melee attack, -1 to all combat bonuses and -10% on skills.', 'Racial skills: Russian and Euro at 70% (+2% per level), Climbing +15%, Detect Concealment +10%, Fishing +10%, Hunting, Identify Plants and Fruit +20%, Land Navigation +20%, Prowl +10%, Skin and Prepare Animal Hides +10%, Swimming +10%, Track and Trap Animals +20%, Tracking (people) +15%, Wilderness Survival +30%, W.P. Spear, Hand to Hand: Basic. A Sovietski soldier adds one military package (Infantry, Reconnaissance or Special Forces); a wild-born one takes seven related skills instead. One Secondary Skill at levels 2, 4, 8 and 14. These and the Cold Born and Wolverine People experience table are on the Wolverine People class.', 'Alarm Howl: three calls (a howl for ordinary danger or a find, a shriek for the supernatural, a bellow for battle or victory) loud enough for a 60% chance (+20% for the shriek) to wake sleepers within 3,000 feet, double downwind; heard two miles off, three downwind. Fast Healing: regains 2D6 M.D.C. per 24 hours of rest, half while fighting or straining, double on a ley line. Impervious to Cold: unaffected down to -50 F; colder takes half penalties and damage, magic cold does half (ice weapons full). Instinctive Fear of the Supernatural. A faint sweet musk. Robot-equivalent strength: a male punch does 1D6 M.D. (claws +6), a power punch 2D6 (power claw 2D6+10), a bite 1D4; a female punch 1D4 (claws +5), power punch 2D4 (power claw 2D4+8), bite 1D4. Superior Sense of Smell: familiar or strong scents 76% +1% per level out to 300 feet per level; unfamiliar or faint ones 50% +2% per level out to 100 feet per level, -25% in snow, fog or light rain, +10% on blood; one roll per 1,000 feet of trail; no tracking through water or heavy rain or snow, and no scenting of astral beings, Entities, ghosts or spirits. Senses and tracking take -25% in cities.', 'None.', 'Minor psychic: Presence Sense, See the Invisible, Sixth Sense, and Sense Evil or Sense Magic. I.S.P. M.E. x3 plus 1D6 per level.', 'Males 6 feet 6 inches to 7 feet 3 inches (1.8 to 2.2 m); females 6 to 7 feet (1.8 to 2.1 m)', 'Males 200 to 400 lbs (90 to 180 kg); females 160 to 250 lbs (72 to 113 kg)', '4D6+50 years; mature at 15', 'Mostly Sovietski territory, moving with the army''s units. Wild loners, pairs, family clans and hunting bands roam Russia, Siberia included, and now and then Scandinavia, Poland and Germany; they favour cold woodland.', 'Sovietski citizens and soldiers stay loyal to the nation for life and count wild Wolverine People as kin. They warm to soldiers, Wilderness Scouts, hunters and people who work with their hands, sculptors among them, and admire poets, storytellers, musicians, dancers and singers.', 'Every enemy of the Sovietski, evil supernatural beings, and anyone who harms them or their kin. They mistrust technology, scientists, technicians, robots, cyborgs and strange-looking aliens, other D-Bees with odd powers, magic or machines most of all.', 'No O.C.C.; they live by their racial skills, a Sovietski military package or, for the wild-born, seven related skills. Playable as the Wolverine People class.', 'Nicknamed Guard Dogs, Russian Yeti or Wolverine Men. Big, fur-covered D-Bees with dark streaked manes, narrow pointed faces, restless ears and amber eyes; males are bearded and shaggy, females sleeker, lighter and quicker but just as lethal. Most serve the Sovietski Army as scouts, trackers, sentries and black-operations troops, raised from childhood in barracks soldiers call the Kennels, and they serve until age or battle ends it. They want little beyond a cot, hot food, vodka and a fight beside their comrades, and treat human soldiers as equals. By nature they flee demons and the like; training turns that into fury. Off duty they are cheerful and boisterous, keen on wrestling, games of skill and dice, and poor singers who sing anyway. Wild clans in the Russian wilderness are rougher, hunt for themselves, trade furs and meat with villagers, and are slow to fight unless wronged, when their revenge can be savage. A soldier or scout sells as a slave for up to 1D4x10,000 credits, a seasoned gladiator for as much as 70,000.', 'Rifts World Book 36: Sovietski p.68-73');

